atible with both systems. Both versions contain exactly the same features. However, their location differs due to differences in how the interaction works.","s":"Introduction iPad","u":"/ianalyse6/en/ipados/ipados-intro","h":"","p":15},{"i":18,"t":"This version of iAnalyse requires the following system: On macOS: 11.0 or higher On iPadOS: iOS 16.6 or higher On iPadOS, it is recommended to have enough memory to store media or to work on a cloud. To use iAnalyse on older macOS systems, download previous versions: https://logiciels.pierrecouprie.fr.","s":"Minimum requirements","u":"/ianalyse6/en/ipados/ipados-intro","h":"#minimum-requirements","p":15},{"i":22,"t":"iAnalyse is a music analysis software program that allows you to create listening guides, annotate audiovisual and MIDI documents, and produce data representations. iAnalyse is presented as a workspace into which you import files (audio, video, images, PDF, MIDI, etc.) and use to create visualizations. You can create multiple documents (slideshows, signal representations, videos, scores) in each iAnalyse project. The documents share the same files. iAnalyse runs on two platforms: macOS and iPadOS. Projects are identical on both platforms and are compatible with both systems. Both versions contain exactly the same features. However, their location differs due to differences in how the interaction works.","s":"Introduction","u":"/ianalyse6/en/macos/macos-intro","h":"","p":21},{"i":24,"t":"This version of iAnalyse requires the following system: On macOS: 11.0 or higher On iPadOS: iOS 16.6 or higher On iPadOS, it is recommended to have enough memory to store media or to work on a cloud. To use iAnalyse on older macOS systems, download previous versions: https://logiciels.pierrecouprie.fr.","s":"Minimum requirements","u":"/ianalyse6/en/macos/macos-intro","h":"#minimum-requirements","p":21}],"index":{"version":"2.3.9","fields":["t"],"fieldVectors":[["t/16",[0,0.166,1,0.593,2,0.593,3,0.593,4,0.593,5,0.593,6,1,7,0.59